# ─── SECRETS — never commit these ───────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
oracle_keys/
ssh-key-*

# ─── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ─── Runtime state (regenerated; not source) ───────────────────────────────
**/data/cache/
**/data/state/
**/data/journal/
**/data/sim/
**/data/reports/
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log
*_service.log

# ─── Local scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.zip
!handoff/*.zip

# C6 (2026-08-07). `handoff/*.zip` is re-included ABOVE ON PURPOSE and that
# decision is what recovered this project: when the Oracle box was
# decommissioned, `handoff/quant_bots.zip` still carried the only copy of
# `options/data/*.py` that git had ever seen. Do not "tidy" that negation away.
#
# The STATE archives are the opposite case — they are a snapshot of runtime
# output, they are not source, and `*.zip` never covered them because they are
# .tgz. `quant_data.tgz` sat untracked AND unignored, one `git add -A` away from
# being committed. Its contents belong in data/journal|sim|reports, which are
# ignored by name above; the archive itself belongs nowhere in git.
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
push_log.txt
